# Bolt Bend (CR 115.7a, 115.7d, rulings 2024-11-08): Bot1's Lightning Bolt targets Bot2's Ornithopter; in response Bot2
# gives it hexproof with Blossoming Defense, so the Bolt's own target is now illegal - "it doesn't matter if the original
# target has somehow become illegal itself". Bot2 then casts Bolt Bend on the Bolt and chooses the new target, but legality
# is judged for the Bolt's controller, Bot1: the hexproof Ornithopter is not among the candidates (the refusal), only Bot1
# and Bot2 are. Bot2 picks itself, so the Bolt takes Bot2 to 17 and the Ornithopter takes no damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Blossoming Defense
Bolt Bend
Island x12

